Z||000003||007DOUG||08-09-2000||12:02 AM||||RobertVol: Just wash them like the others. If scratches ever appear they can be removed with plastic polish. (Same goes for GM originals)<P>I've never heard of anyone having problems with fit, however these are prototypes of the "second generation" windows, so anything's possible right now.<P>You'll have another window on the way tomorrow.<P>Gosh, I hope yours is the only one. That's making me nervous.<P>Cooter, Dan? How's yours?<P>Al, I know you love yours. Thanx<P>So can we all agree on this: You won't get any closer to originals unless you BUY originals. <P>Whew, this is as close as i'm going to try and get. <P>------------------<BR>4 Indy pace Cars<BR>84 T-top<BR>84 SE<BR>86 SE V6<BR>2 86 GT's<BR>86 GT 3.4 Pearl White T-top<BR>2 88 GT twins<P>However......<BR><I>"Time is my most precious and most perishable of all my possessions."</I>||||reg||6
